"""Fine-tune Vocos on mels generated by the trained TTS model ("GTA" fine-tuning, ``finetune-vocoder``).

The frozen TTS model produces mels for training utterances under the *ground-truth* alignment (teacher-forced
durations and pitch), so every generated frame lines up with the recorded waveform. Vocos is then trained to turn
the model's (smoother) mels into the real audio with its GAN objective: fresh multi-period and multi-resolution
discriminators (none were released), hinge loss, feature matching and an L1 log-mel loss, after a discriminator
warm-up. On BigVGAN-style mels its ISTFT head uses ``same`` padding, which centres frame ``i`` on sample
``i * hop + hop / 2`` as BigVGAN's uncentred STFT does.

Recipes: ``configs/vocos_v1.yaml`` (the Vocos recipe, 40k steps: ``vocos-ft``), ``configs/vocos_v2.yaml``
(continued 160k steps with rebalanced discriminators, the multi-scale mel loss, an instantaneous-frequency loss and a
cosine schedule: ``vocos-v2``) and ``configs/vocos_v2_balance.yaml`` (20k more steps on speaker-balanced batches:
``vocos-v2-balanced``). ``train.speaker_balance`` (opt-in) gives chosen speakers fixed shares of the batches and splits
the rest over the other speakers by their amount of audio raised to a temperature (:func:`batch_sampler`).
The exported ``vocos_ft.pt`` loads with :func:`fast_tr_drifting.vocoder.load_vocoder`. The trainer uses the ``vocos``
package (its discriminators and losses; ``pip install fast-tr-drifting[train]``).
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import math
import shutil
import time
import warnings
from pathlib import Path

import torch
import torch.nn.functional as F
from torch import Tensor, nn
from torch.utils.data import DataLoader

